IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-cpc-interface`

-- Criminal Procedure Code 2010 (2020 Revised Edition), Singapore Statutes Online,
-- current version as at 01 Oct 2026.
-- Source: source/CPC2010.txt (extracted from source/CPC2010.pdf); line references in the other modules are to that
-- file.  The First Schedule is read from the PDF by position (generators/first_schedule_extract.py), not from the text.
--
-- The shared nouns, and nothing else: DECLARE only, no rules, no #EVAL.  Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this fact, or does answering it require reading
-- the Code?  Only the first kind is a field here.  "The police officer is of or above the rank of sergeant" is a fact;
-- "the offence is an arrestable offence" is a rule (it is read off the First Schedule or another written law).
--
-- SCOPE: this row encodes the First Schedule ("Tabular statement of offences under the Penal Code 1871") and the provisions that
-- read it directly: section 2(1) (arrestable, non-arrestable, bailable, fine-only) and sections 7 to 9 (trial courts).  The rest of the
-- Code, and the Second to Seventh Schedules, are not encoded: NOTES.md section 2.
--
-- ea-cpc-interface.l4 is carried because the Evidence Act subject needs an identical copy; nothing in this row's rules reads it yet.

§ `The First Schedule: a tabular statement of offences under the Penal Code 1871`

-- Columns 3, 4, 5 and 7 of the printed table are controlled phrases.  Where the printed cell is not a fixed answer but says "as
-- for the offence" abetted, conspired in, attempted or otherwise the subject of the row, the cell is `As for the underlying
-- offence` and the row's `derivation note` carries the printed words.
@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, First Schedule column 3; section 2(1) 'arrestable offence', 'non-arrestable offence'"
DECLARE `Arrest Rule` IS ONE OF
    `May arrest without warrant`
    `May not arrest without warrant`
    `May not arrest without warrant unless specifically empowered by the law offended against`
    `As for the underlying offence`

@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, First Schedule column 4"
DECLARE `Process Rule` IS ONE OF
    `A warrant ordinarily issues`
    `A summons ordinarily issues`
    `As for the underlying offence`
    `As for the offence committed by the person hired, engaged or employed`

@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, First Schedule column 5; section 2(1) 'bailable offence'"
DECLARE `Bail Rule` IS ONE OF
    `Bailable`
    `Not bailable`
    `As for the underlying offence`

@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, First Schedule column 7; sections 7, 8, 9"
DECLARE `Court Rule` IS ONE OF
    `Magistrate's Court or District Court`
    `District Court`
    `General Division of the High Court only`
    `As for the underlying offence`
    `According to sections 7, 8 and 9`

@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, First Schedule"
DECLARE `First Schedule Row` HAS
    `printed section` IS A STRING
    `base section` IS A STRING
    `offence description` IS A STRING
    `arrest rule` IS AN `Arrest Rule`
    `process rule` IS A `Process Rule`
    `bail rule` IS A `Bail Rule`
    `maximum punishment` IS A STRING
    `court rule` IS A `Court Rule`
    `chapter heading` IS A STRING
    `derivation note` IS A STRING
    `page of the SSO PDF` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, First Schedule; sections 2(1), 9(2), 9(3), 153(1), 153(3), 226(5)"
DECLARE `Procedural Treatment` HAS
    `the police may ordinarily arrest without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a warrant ordinarily issues in the first instance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is bailable of right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Magistrate's Court may try the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a District Court may try the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the General Division of the High Court may try the offence` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 2 -- Criminal jurisdiction of State Courts (sections 7 to 9, which read the First Schedule's seventh column)`

@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, ss 2(1) 'fine-only offence', 7(1)(a), 8(1), 9(1), 9(2), 9(3)"
DECLARE `Jurisdiction Facts` HAS
    `the offence is punishable with death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is a fine-only offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maximum term of imprisonment provided by law, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the offence is under the Penal Code 1871` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the First Schedule shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the First Schedule shows the offence as triable by a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a law other than the Penal Code 1871 shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a law other than the Penal Code 1871 shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Prosecutor has authorised in writing a Magistrate's Court to try the offence in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Prosecutor applies to the District Court to try the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused consents, or if more than one are charged together with the same offence, all consent` IS A BOOLEAN
